			},
			"date": "2026-09-27T20:00:12.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Yeah I framed houses for a few months as a summer job once. One day I measured one opening and made some cuts to use for it and for another identical opening. The wood I cut didn't fit in the second. The pro said \"why didn't you measure both?\" I said \"in theory, aren't they supposed to be the same?\" He said \"yeah theory doesn't work. You need to measure both\", and that really stuck wtih me.</p><p>Anyway, sorry for your dissapointment!! I feel ya ✌🏻</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
